    <custom_item>
      type        : CMD_EXEC
      description : "1.131 APPL-26-004001"
      info        : "The macOS system must configure Apple System Log (ASL) files owned by root and group to wheel.

GROUP ID: V-277158
RULE ID: SV-277158r1148926

The ASL must be owned by root.

ASLs contain sensitive data about the system and users. Setting ASL files to be readable and writable only by system administrators mitigates the risk.

Satisfies: SRG-OS-000205-GPOS-00083, SRG-OS-000206-GPOS-00084"
      solution    : "Configure the macOS system with ASL files owned by root and group to wheel with the following command:

/usr/sbin/chown root:wheel $(/usr/bin/stat -f '%Su:%Sg:%N' $(/usr/bin/grep -e '^>' /etc/asl.conf /etc/asl/* | /usr/bin/awk '{ print $2 }') 2> /dev/null | /usr/bin/awk '!/^root:wheel:/{print $1}' | /usr/bin/awk -F\":\" '!/^root:wheel:/{print $3}')"
      reference   : "800-53|SI-11a.,800-53|SI-11b.,800-53r5|SI-11,800-53r5|SI-11a.,800-53r5|SI-11b.,CCI|CCI-001312,CCI|CCI-001314,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ITSG-33|SI-11b.,ITSG-33|SI-11c.,LEVEL|2A,Rule-ID|SV-277158r1148926_rule,STIG-ID|APPL-26-004001,Vuln-ID|V-277158"
      see_also    : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/26538"
      cmd         : "/usr/bin/stat -f '%Su:%Sg:%N' $(/usr/bin/grep -e '^>' /etc/asl.conf /etc/asl/* | /usr/bin/awk '{ print $2 }') 2> /dev/null | /usr/bin/awk '!/^root:wheel:/{print $1}' | /usr/bin/wc -l | /usr/bin/tr -d ''"
      expect      : "^0$"
    </custom_item>

    <custom_item>
      type        : CMD_EXEC
      description : "1.132 APPL-26-004002"
      info        : "The macOS system must configure Apple System Log (ASL) files to mode 640 or less permissive.

GROUP ID: V-277159
RULE ID: SV-277159r1148929

The ASLs must be configured to be writable by root and readable only by the root user and group wheel. To achieve this, ASL files must be configured to mode 640 permissive or less, thereby preventing normal users from reading, modifying, or deleting audit logs.

System logs frequently contain sensitive information that could be used by an attacker. Setting the correct permissions mitigates this risk.

Satisfies: SRG-OS-000205-GPOS-00083, SRG-OS-000206-GPOS-00084"
      solution    : "Configure the macOS system with ASL files to mode 640 with the following command:

/bin/chmod 640 $(/usr/bin/stat -f '%A:%N' $(/usr/bin/grep -e '^>' /etc/asl.conf /etc/asl/* | /usr/bin/awk '{ print $2 }') 2> /dev/null | /usr/bin/awk -F\":\" '!/640/{print $2}')"
      reference   : "800-53|SI-11a.,800-53|SI-11b.,800-53r5|SI-11,800-53r5|SI-11a.,800-53r5|SI-11b.,CCI|CCI-001312,CCI|CCI-001314,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ITSG-33|SI-11b.,ITSG-33|SI-11c.,LEVEL|2A,Rule-ID|SV-277159r1148929_rule,STIG-ID|APPL-26-004002,Vuln-ID|V-277159"
      see_also    : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/26538"
      cmd         : "/usr/bin/stat -f '%A:%N' $(/usr/bin/grep -e '^>' /etc/asl.conf /etc/asl/* | /usr/bin/awk '{ print $2 }') 2> /dev/null | /usr/bin/awk '!/640/{print $1}' | /usr/bin/wc -l | /usr/bin/tr -d ' '"
