    <custom_item>
      type        : CMD_EXEC
      description : "1.49 APPL-26-001031"
      info        : "The macOS system must configure audit failure notification.

GROUP ID: V-277076
RULE ID: SV-277076r1148680

The audit service must be configured to immediately print messages to the console or email administrator users when an auditing failure occurs.

It is critical for the appropriate personnel to be made aware immediately if a system is at risk of failing to process audit logs as required. Without a real-time alert, security personnel may be unaware of a potentially harmful failure in the auditing system's capability, and system operation may be adversely affected."
      solution    : "Configure the macOS system to produce audit failure notification with the following command:

/usr/bin/sed -i.bak 's/logger -p/logger -s -p/' /etc/security/audit_warn; /usr/sbin/audit -s"
      reference   : "800-171|3.3.4,800-171r3|03.03.04,800-53|AU-5(2),800-53r5|AU-5(2),CCI|CCI-001858,CN-L3|7.1.3.3(e),CSF|PR.PT-1,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),HIPAA|164.312(b),ITSG-33|AU-5(2),LEVEL|2A,NESA|T3.6.2,NIAv2|GS7f,QCSC-v1|8.2.1,QCSC-v1|13.2,Rule-ID|SV-277076r1148680_rule,STIG-ID|APPL-26-001031,Vuln-ID|V-277076"
      see_also    : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/26538"
      cmd         : "/usr/bin/grep -c \"logger -s -p\" /etc/security/audit_warn"
      expect      : "^1$"
    </custom_item>

    <custom_item>
      type        : CMD_EXEC
      description : "1.5 APPL-26-000007"
      info        : "The macOS system must disable hot corners.

GROUP ID: V-277032
RULE ID: SV-277032r1148548

Hot corners must be disabled.

The information system conceals, via the session lock, information previously visible on the display with a publicly viewable image. Although hot corners can be used to initiate a session lock or to launch useful applications, they can also be configured to disable an automatic session lock from initiating. Such a configuration introduces the risk that a user might forget to manually lock the screen before stepping away from the computer."
      solution    : "Configure the macOS system to disable hot corners by installing the \"com.apple.ManagedClient.preferences\" configuration profile."
      reference   : "800-171|3.1.10,800-171r3|03.01.10,800-53|AC-11(1),800-53r5|AC-11(1),CCI|CCI-000060,CN-L3|8.1.4.1(b),GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),HIPAA|164.312(a)(2)(iii),ISO-27001-2022|A.7.7,ISO-27001-2022|A.8.1,ISO/IEC-27001|A.11.2.8,ITSG-33|AC-11(1),LEVEL|2A,NIAv2|AM23c,NIAv2|AM23d,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|8.1.8,PCI-DSSv4.0|8.2.8,Rule-ID|SV-277032r1148548_rule,STIG-ID|APPL-26-000007,Vuln-ID|V-277032"
      see_also    : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/26538"
      cmd         : "/usr/bin/profiles -P -o stdout | /usr/bin/grep -Ec '\"wvous-bl-corner\" = 0|\"wvous-br-corner\" = 0|\"wvous-tl-corner\" = 0|\"wvous-tr-corner\" = 0'"
      expect      : "^4$"
    </custom_item>

    <custom_item>
      type        : CMD_EXEC
      description : "1.50 APPL-26-001044"
      info        : "The macOS system must be configured to audit all authorization and authentication events.

GROUP ID: V-277077
RULE ID: SV-277077r1148683

The auditing system must be configured to flag authorization and authentication (aa) events.

Authentication events contain information about the identity of a user, server, or client. Authorization events contain information about permissions, rights, and rules. If audit records do not include aa events, it is difficult to identify incidents and correlate incidents to subsequent events.

Audit records can be generated from various components within the information system (e.g., via a module or policy filter).

Satisfies: SRG-OS-000365-GPOS-00152, SRG-OS-000392-GPOS-00172, SRG-OS-000458-GPOS-00203, SRG-OS-000463-GPOS-00207, SRG-OS-000465-GPOS-00209, SRG-OS-000466-GPOS-00210, SRG-OS-000467-GPOS-00211, SRG-OS-000468-GPOS-00212, SRG-OS-000471-GPOS-00215, SRG-OS-000471-GPOS-00216, SRG-OS-000475-GPOS-00220, SRG-OS-000477-GPOS-00222"
      solution    : "Configure the macOS system to audit login events with the following command:

/usr/bin/grep -qE \"^flags.*[^-]aa\" /etc/security/audit_control || /usr/bin/sed -i.bak '/^flags/ s/$/,aa/' /etc/security/audit_control; /usr/sbin/audit -s"
      reference   : "800-171|3.3.1,800-171|3.3.2,800-171|3.7.5,800-171r3|03.03.03a.,800-171r3|03.07.05,800-53|AU-12c.,800-53|MA-4(1),800-53r5|AU-12c.,800-53r5|CM-5(1),800-53r5|MA-4(1),CCI|CCI-000172,CCI|CCI-002884,CCI|CCI-003938,CN-L3|7.1.3.3(a),CN-L3|7.1.3.3(b),CN-L3|7.1.3.3(c),CN-L3|8.1.3.5(a),CN-L3|8.1.3.5(b),CN-L3|8.1.4.3(a),CSF|DE.CM-1,CSF|DE.CM-3,CSF|DE.CM-7,CSF|PR.MA-2,CSF|PR.PT-1,CSF2.0|DE.CM-01,CSF2.0|DE.CM-03,CSF2.0|DE.CM-09,CSF2.0|PR.PS-04,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),HIPAA|164.312(b),ISO-27001-2022|A.8.15,ISO-27001-2022|A.8.16,ISO/IEC-27001|A.12.4.1,ITSG-33|AU-12c.,ITSG-33|MA-4(1),LEVEL|2A,NESA|T2.3.4,NESA|T3.6.2,NESA|T3.6.5,NESA|T3.6.6,NIAv2|SM8,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|10.1,QCSC-v1|3.2,QCSC-v1|5.2.2,QCSC-v1|6.2,QCSC-v1|8.2.1,QCSC-v1|13.2,Rule-ID|SV-277077r1148683_rule,STIG-ID|APPL-26-001044,SWIFT-CSCv1|6.4,TBA-FIISB|45.1.1,TBA-FIISB|45.2.3,Vuln-ID|V-277077"
      see_also    : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/26538"
