    <custom_item>
      type         : MACOSX_OSASCRIPT
      description  : "1.6 APPL-26-000009"
      info         : "The macOS system must prevent AdminHostInfo from being available at LoginWindow.

GROUP ID: V-277033
RULE ID: SV-277033r1149397

The system must be configured to not display sensitive information at the LoginWindow. If the key \"AdminHostInfo\" is configured with a string value, it will allow the HostName, IP Address, and operating system version and build to be displayed when clicking on the clock area of the login window. Configuring this key to be an integer value, since it expects a string value, will effectively disable the behavior.

Note: This configuration requires it to be deployed via Managed Preferences rather than directly to com.apple.loginwindow."
      solution     : "Configure the macOS system to prevent AdminHostInfo from being available at LoginWindow by installing the \"com.apple.ManagedClient.preferences\" configuration profile."
      reference    : "800-171|3.1.10,800-171r3|03.01.10,800-53|AC-11(1),800-53r5|AC-11(1),CCI|CCI-000060,CN-L3|8.1.4.1(b),GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),HIPAA|164.312(a)(2)(iii),ISO-27001-2022|A.7.7,ISO-27001-2022|A.8.1,ISO/IEC-27001|A.11.2.8,ITSG-33|AC-11(1),LEVEL|2A,NIAv2|AM23c,NIAv2|AM23d,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|8.1.8,PCI-DSSv4.0|8.2.8,Rule-ID|SV-277033r1149397_rule,STIG-ID|APPL-26-000009,Vuln-ID|V-277033"
